.TH HUFFMAN 1 "July 28, 2026" "huffman" "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
huffman \- command-line Huffman encoder and decoder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B huffman
[\fB\-d\fR] [\fB\-p\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads raw data from standard input, applies or reverses Huffman
encoding, and writes the result to standard output.  This is an
educational, toy implementation aimed at clarity rather than
production-grade compression.  For real-world use, prefer gzip(1)
or lzma(1).

It is however made to be as fast as possible with the compression ratio offered
by huffman encoding
.P
When invoked without flags,
.B huffman
operates in encode mode: it builds a Huffman tree from the byte
frequencies of the input, generates canonical codes, and writes a
compressed bitstream prefixed by a header that lists each distinct
character and its code length.
.P
The container format is:
.IP \(bu 2
Byte 0: number of unique characters minus 1 (0\(en255).
.IP \(bu 2
For each character, sorted by canonical code length ascending: the
character byte, followed by its code length in bits (1\(en255).
.IP \(bu 2
The remaining bytes form the canonical Huffman bitstream, most
significant bit first within each byte, arbitrarily padded.
.P
In decode mode (\fB\-d\fR) the header and bitstream are read back,
the canonical codes are reconstructed from the stored code lengths,
and the original data is recovered.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-d
Decode (decompress) mode.  Read a previously compressed stream from
standard input and write the decompressed result to standard output.
.TP
.B \-p
Enable debug printing.  Frequency tables, tree structure, canonical
codes, and per-character serialization details are written to
standard error.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.IP 0
Successful completion.
.IP 1
A fatal error occurred (e.g. malformed compressed input).
.SH EXAMPLES
Compress a file:
.RS
.PD 0
.P
huffman < document.txt > document.huf
.PD
.RE
.P
Decompress a file:
.RS
.PD 0
.P
huffman -d < document.huf > document.txt
.PD
.RE
.P
Compress, pipe through decompression, and run the result:
.RS
.PD 0
.P
huffman < /bin/ls | huffman -d > ls
.P
chmod +x ./ls && ./ls
.PD
.RE
.P
Inspect internal state during compression or decompression:
.RS
.PD 0
.P
huffman -p < document.txt > /dev/null
.P
huffman -pd < document.huf > /dev/null
.PD
.RE
.SH BUGS
The debug output is written via
.BR printf (3)
and can therefore interleave with compressed data sent to standard
output when both streams share a terminal.
.P
Report bugs and submit patches to
.UR https://github.com/abvee/huffman
.UE .
.SH AUTHOR
abvee
